            mutable this: Planner,
            prefix: String,
            mutable suffix: String,
            arg_types: Vector[PlannedType],
            arg_ops: Vector[PlannedOperand]
        ) @page true @direct true @stores true @deep true @deep_this_8 true returns ref[MethodMatch]? io linked

        ; concept_has_static: does `prefix` name a Structure concept declaring a
        ; this-LESS (static) member function called `suffix`? A qualified call
        ; `Type.method(...)` on such a concept is a static call that MUST carry
        ; the concept parent in its mangled name — the s155 concept-static path
        ; (gated match_ref=null in collapse_operand_sequence#) does exactly that.
        ; resolve_dotted_call# defers to it (returns null) for these, so the
        ; bare-suffix resolve below can never mis-match an unrelated same-named
        ; free function. This is load-bearing for opensp: every module exposes a
        ; `test()` static and the function-only ones ALSO register `test` in the
        ; free registry (register_concept_recursive's Namespace arm), so a bare
        ; `test` resolve returns SOME `test` and `StringC.test()` mis-mangled to
        ; the enclosing/sibling `test` — the aggregator self-recursed. Gated to
        ; Structures only: Namespace-member calls (Console.println) keep their
        ; existing bare-then-namespace resolution untouched.
        procedure concept_has_static(mutable this: Planner, prefix: String, suffix: String) @ret_nonlocal true @deep true returns bool linked

        ; s-LSP: the dotted-call fallback's resolution, as ONE call so the
        ; caller (collapse_operand_sequence#) keeps a single `set match_ref:`
        ; statement — adding a branch there perturbed its s178 alloca pool.
        ; Try the normal this-implicit overload first; if that misses, try the
        ; namespace this-method-with-explicit-receiver form.
        ; ★★★The OPERANDS travel with the types since 2026-09-06. Both resolves
        ; below used to hand resolve_function_call# an EMPTY operand vector, and
        ; every literal fallback of the matcher (the char fold, the float retype,
        ; the string-literal-into-Slice[char] materialisation) asks the OPERAND
        ; whether it is a constant -- with no operands in hand the fallback pass
        ; never matched, and a NAMESPACE function taking a `Slice[char]` could
        ; not be reached by a literal at all: `Planner.make_primitive_type("void",
        ; "v")` was a hard "function not found" while the identical call on a
        ; Structure's static resolved (that path selects by name and arity and
        ; folds at the construction site). Found converting the compiler's own
        ; ASCII-literal parameters; gate `tests/regress/namespace_literal_slice_arg.scaly`.
